when the scene loads one currency loads first then the second one. I want to remove the delay and optimise the code

response_ctrl:
To make both currencies display at the same time, you can use async tasks and the "await Task.WhenAll()" method to get the player balances simultaneously. Here's an optimized version of your code:

```csharp
private async void LoadAllCurrencies()
{
    List<CurrencyDefinition> definitions = await EconomyService.Instance.Configuration.GetCurrenciesAsync();

    // Set up tasks to query balances for both FOX_COIN and FANTASY_DIAMOND
    Task<PlayerBalance> softCurrencyTask = null;
    Task<PlayerBalance> premiumCurrencyTask = null;

    foreach (CurrencyDefinition currency in definitions)
    {
        if (currency.Id.ToString() == "FOX_COIN")
        {
            softCurrencyTask = currency.GetPlayerBalanceAsync();
        }
        else if (currency.Id.ToString() == "FANTASY_DIAMOND")
        {
            premiumCurrencyTask = currency.GetPlayerBalanceAsync();
        }
    }

    // Wait for both balance queries to complete
    await Task.WhenAll(softCurrencyTask, premiumCurrencyTask);

    // Update the UI with the balances
    if (softCurrencyTask != null)
    {
        softCurrency.text = softCurrencyTask.Result.Balance.ToString();
    }
    if (premiumCurrencyTask != null)
    {
        premiumCurrency.text = premiumCurrencyTask.Result.Balance.ToString();
    }
}
```

By using `Task.WhenAll()` you ensure both player balance queries run in parallel, removing the need to wait for one to complete before starting the other. This should make the display of both currencies more efficient.

